\name{cellucid_highlight_group_toggle}
\alias{cellucid_highlight_group_toggle}
\title{Show or hide a highlight group}
\usage{
cellucid_highlight_group_toggle(viewer, group, enabled, page)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{group}{A highlight group, by its label as the group list shows it (without the cell count). Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
\item{enabled}{true to show the group, false to hide it. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Required.}
\item{page}{The group's page, by name; omitted, the page shown. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Turn one group of a page on or off; a group that is off highlights nothing.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{highlight.group.toggle} (Highlights). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{highlights}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_highlight_group_toggle(viewer,
      enabled = FALSE, group = "x")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
